{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwufqPVnRoeUkyvpPu42","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I estimated the ATT by regression adjustment. The data has no true counterfactuals, so this is an estimate and depends on the model. I fit an OLS outcome model on the control group only, using all 25 covariates. I then predicted the untreated outcome for each treated child and averaged the gap between observed and predicted outcomes.\n\n| Method | Estimate |\n|---|---|\n| Raw difference in means (treated minus control, no adjustment) | 12.10 |\n| OLS with a treatment indicator and all covariates (closer to an ATE) | 4.76 |\n| Control-only outcome model, averaged over the treated (ATT) | 3.80 |\n\nThe raw difference is much larger, which suggests the treated and control groups differ on the covariates. I chose the control-only model because it targets the effect on the treated group specifically.\n\nANSWER: 3.80"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":31401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":385},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"270b68ac-14e1-46ff-b937-a52284e5deeb","uuid":"a619d4a6-6aa9-4717-a2dc-ed2280a00acc","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:12:42.355Z","request_id":"req_011Cgwufq7PBv6yShNmmELmw"}
